oters torched public buildings and looted shops across France, destroying Limoges' historic town hall. The violence erupted during nationwide cost-of-living protests.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Vietnam signs free trade deal with four European countries</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9fbe5cc13d7a2ffdc420e2bb6ea8a70a2b926717b52ee7f3ff5e823ff9f9d892</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T09:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/vietnam-signs-free-trade-deal-with-four-european-countries/a-79691812--7e41481b6a6a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/vietnam-signs-free-trade-deal-with-four-european-countries/a-79691812?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Vietnam has signed a deal with four non-EU members that covers trade in goods and services, intellectual property rights, and sustainable development, among other areas.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>How reliant is Ukraine on the US-controlled Starlink internet service?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e15be590d2c01913e64f8dc8e8619d72dcff719a539cbae7fdb6aae7bb45f506</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:41:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T08:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-reliant-is-ukraine-on-the-us-controlled-starlink-internet-service/a-79689729--6217d664b01d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-reliant-is-ukraine-on-the-us-controlled-starlink-internet-service/a-79689729?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Kyiv keeps issuing warnings that the satellite internet system Starlink is being restricted in Ukraine. How dependent is the country on the system, and what would happen if it went down?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Police probe security incident at Leipzig/Halle airport</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:43f9df1b80022feb74cb6d1a37c728c007df5f3997dd20db0b1e839f794b2abf</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:41:20Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T08:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-police-probe-security-incident-at-leipzig-halle-airport/live-79686913--f152414b1a9b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-police-probe-security-incident-at-leipzig-halle-airport/live-79686913?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A fence breach at the Leipzig/Halle airport has triggered a major police operation. Christian Social Union leader Markus Söder is to address a gathering of the conservative youth wing. Follow DW for more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Populist Czech PM Babis goes empty-handed in Senate elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:38b48925de53eeb967397a8453446c14e74d872a85fafb0927585a21f6fe080f</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:41:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T07:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/populist-czech-pm-babis-goes-empty-handed-in-senate-elections/a-79690934--95037aa1aa28.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/populist-czech-pm-babis-goes-empty-handed-in-senate-elections/a-79690934?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Opposition parties still control the Czech Senate, in a major blow to Prime Minister Andrej Babis' and his governing coalition.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India: CJP leader Abhijeet Dipke released after detention</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:03ec11b5923cf5245474e18402cd92406255ec1ae8c99b5ebdb55168b89d4aa1</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:41:27Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T06:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-cjp-leader-abhijeet-dipke-released-after-detention/a-79690933--80500fd3a662.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-cjp-leader-abhijeet-dipke-released-after-detention/a-79690933?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two other prominent CJP leaders are set to be released on Sunday. India has seen huge rallies calling on the country's top election official to step down over alleged manipulation of voter rolls.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Kolkata stampede dampens Durga Puja festivities</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bc828dbff573f28389a53be266e81349454459bcec00a43dd9bbb3a43bbcedb8</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T04:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-kolkata-stampede-dampens-durga-puja-festivities/live-79685143--9e78a7d0cccd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-kolkata-stampede-dampens-durga-puja-festivities/live-79685143?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Authorities have detained several people over a deadly stampede in India's eastern city of Kolkata, after the state vowed strict action. Meanwhile, 'Cockroach' leader Dipke is out of detention. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Canada: Major fire reported at military base in Alberta</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ad1a6f8a8a3e399dd40cc7b164101f9292c6ed028a719d62078f8984a1e02f94</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T02:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/canada-major-fire-reported-at-military-base-in-alberta/a-79690515--194f6f97e468.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/canada-major-fire-reported-at-military-base-in-alberta/a-79690515?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney has said a "serious incident" sparked a major fire at a military base in Alberta. He did not provide details on the cause of the fire.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>'No Kings' rallies push early voting ahead of US midterm elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:adb95c97985b85dfea053d638c6dddd3f0a2395ce24f05c664a032f554fa1c1d</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T00:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/no-kings-rallies-push-early-voting-ahead-of-us-midterm-elections/a-79690502--c2c75c7f5f7c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/no-kings-rallies-push-early-voting-ahead-of-us-midterm-elections/a-79690502?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Organizers of the "No Kings" protests, known for their anti-Trump sentiment, are urging Americans to vote early in the November 3 midterm elections, as Republicans face tough races to retain control of Congress.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ilhan Omar: The US Democrat targeted by Donald Trump</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1e00b4a163c25552afff3a907b1cb65e37e9a06a0be1ae0519874362826541da</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T19:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ilhan-omar-the-us-democrat-targeted-by-donald-trump/a-79688445--0b2fbb5ba398.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ilhan-omar-the-us-democrat-targeted-by-donald-trump/a-79688445?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump has described her as "garbage" and a "criminal" who does nothing but "bitch." Congress member Ilhan Omar has long been the target of angry verbal attacks from the US president. But why her?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Romanian fighter jets shoot down 2 drones over Black Sea</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4e981d57c0cf3770c3687e6bef2c58eeba66d72765444b5bf4abc731187f2a36</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T17:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/romanian-fighter-jets-shoot-down-2-drones-over-black-sea/a-79689156--bd62b985e5d3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/romanian-fighter-jets-shoot-down-2-drones-over-black-sea/a-79689156?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Romanian Air Force F-16s shot down drones over Romanian territorial waters. Earlier this week, two chemical tankers were hit by drones near Romania's Black Sea coast.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Egypt's Ssisi says he'll defend Saudi Arabia, if asked</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3c82869faf186f030d985966c5ae98b65a32e2f30777c8d241cfd17b76f106be</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T17:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/egypt-s-ssisi-says-he-ll-defend-saudi-arabia-if-asked/a-79689105--a11b59189924.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/egypt-s-ssisi-says-he-ll-defend-saudi-arabia-if-asked/a-79689105?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Egyptian president said his country was ready to defend Saudi Arabia "if requested." The comments come amid escalating Houthi attacks.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>West Bank: Israeli settlers attack EU diplomats, French mayor</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a5b8eea0df0637efd91249f4de4b6ead0d3942319588683cc38c8c4f1957d655</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T16:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/west-bank-israeli-settlers-attack-eu-diplomats-french-mayor/a-79688819--13df4c5f717b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/west-bank-israeli-settlers-attack-eu-diplomats-french-mayor/a-79688819?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A group of Israeli settlers attacked vehicles carrying European diplomats in the West Bank, a day after an American photographer was beaten. Belgium and France have condemned the attack.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>How big is Russia's threat against Germany?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:95dca309973523d68a409504af237ae734788ad3f508c5ee6d1acb38616f629b</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T15:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-big-is-russia-s-threat-against-germany/a-79688426--e8db9669a70a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-big-is-russia-s-threat-against-germany/a-79688426?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Experts believe that, so far, Germany has been ill-prepared — both militarily and mentally — for Russian provocations. They also warn against the idea that ending support for Ukraine would make Germany safer.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>China's influence in the gaming industry is growing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6d963edd8250af21753546393471dbd385478827df4308249a56c423a7914600</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T14:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-s-influence-in-the-gaming-industry-is-growing/a-79484755--447380e7608a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-s-influence-in-the-gaming-industry-is-growing/a-79484755?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Home to more than 700 million gamers, China is the world's largest gaming market — but it's also one of the most tightly regulated. The effects reach far beyond China, impacting players around the world.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo leaves hospital after cancer surgery</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8646493dd861661d61982ddf124d8447befd61ed7f6507aa3cdf3beca60335af</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T13:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pope-leo-leaves-hospital-after-cancer-surgery/a-79688162--69f6144ccc39.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pope-leo-leaves-hospital-after-cancer-surgery/a-79688162?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Four days after undergoing surgery for lung cancer, Pope Leo left the hospital in Rome. His doctors said he was well enough to return home.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russia wants blackout in Ukraine as winter comes — Zelenskyy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ab099fd779d7dc73895e4f1e6bbe7a4f7504e6fe8385105db32669823b0bb404</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T11:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-wants-blackout-in-ukraine-as-winter-comes-zelenskyy/a-79686703--c66cb23b1a91.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-wants-blackout-in-ukraine-as-winter-comes-zelenskyy/a-79686703?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Zelenskyy says Russia is trying to cut electricity and heating to civilians ahead of winter. He also called the US president's waiver of new sanctions on Moscow a boost for Vladimir Putin.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Mexico sentences killers of US, Australian surfers to 158 years each in prison</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7284a048a4effcdd66acfa1f04e4d4503184fbfdc4b9fb29a21a189544fed2cb</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T08:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/mexico-sentences-killers-of-us-australian-surfers-to-158-years-each-in-prison/a-79685975--d9f256fde01a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/mexico-sentences-killers-of-us-australian-surfers-to-158-years-each-in-prison/a-79685975?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Three Mexican men were found guilty last week of murdering foreign surfers in 2024. The case had drawn global condemnation, particularly in Australia, where two of the victims were from.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>France: Protesters clash with police in nationwide protests, amid rising social polarization</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fc649f9a0cb9378310068a1c070b62a5a379fdc24c52fd81f19b37ab6efb8c6d</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T08:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-protesters-clash-with-police-in-nationwide-protests-amid-rising-social-polarization/a-79685584--b410e6f9b726.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-protesters-clash-with-police-in-nationwide-protests-amid-rising-social-polarization/a-79685584?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Unrest broke out in parts of France as students, trade unionists and Yellow Vest activists took to the streets to protest high prices and inequality. Police arrested over 1,000 people amid chaotic scenes.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ukrainian President Zelenskyy speaks at EU summit amid spat with Donald Trump</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7c943f5e7891b36eb226ba1caefd7d8dfcbda6369c9632a92a30b85352f0cb4a</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T19:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukrainian-president-zelenskyy-speaks-at-eu-summit-amid-spat-with-donald-trump/a-79684340--6307cb90b3ba.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukrainian-president-zelenskyy-speaks-at-eu-summit-amid-spat-with-donald-trump/a-79684340?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">EU leaders reaffirmed support for Ukraine at the Brussels summit. But souring relations with the US over Russia and Starlink and a big hole in the budget will make for a difficult winter for Ukraine.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Hijab ban at schools in Azerbaijan: What's behind the rare wave of protests?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:660e6af1b6db68964063003ad8149f589dd044b7a25cbf3d44592274cb4f1fcb</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T17:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hijab-ban-at-schools-in-azerbaijan-what-s-behind-the-rare-wave-of-protests/a-79683716--35e52a17baf3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hijab-ban-at-schools-in-azerbaijan-what-s-behind-the-rare-wave-of-protests/a-79683716?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Girls wearing headscarves have been turned away from schools in Azerbaijan, triggering unusual protests involving children. The government rules do not mention hijabs. Why are schools enforcing unwritten rules?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>The Bundestag has debated the genocide Germany carried out in Namibia a century ago. But will it spur progress on addressing colonial crimes?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4db8aceb51374e02205bcb47ff3bf2a8b080cf88a99a6cacfe010b8d9550f650</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T14:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-bundestag-has-debated-the-genocide-germany-carried-out-in-namibia-a-century-ago-but-will-it-spur/a-79682388--50aa326f1793.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-bundestag-has-debated-the-genocide-germany-carried-out-in-namibia-a-century-ago-but-will-it-spur-progress-on-addressing-colonial-crimes/a-79682388?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Opposition parties have forced a debate in the Bundestag on the early-20th-century genocide Germany carried out in Namibia. Will this finally spur progress in addressing colonial crimes?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Albania: Students demand political change and resignation of Prime Minister Edi Rama</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ee64c9a9f7c35817509ccbbecb6f1aa95f4096916bbe6d23ae31a4f0bdfc0541</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T14:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/albania-students-demand-political-change-and-resignation-of-prime-minister-edi-rama/a-79682217--699ae649993b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/albania-students-demand-political-change-and-resignation-of-prime-minister-edi-rama/a-79682217?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Empty lecture halls, burning buildings and demands for change: Albanian students are spearheading a protest movement that has become the biggest challenge to Prime Minister Edi Rama in years.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>The EU wants an AI revolution. But on whose terms?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f063eb0816694904176dbcbc7ff06edac026d54595b0bf7229efa98c7bc64dc8</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T13:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-eu-wants-an-ai-revolution-but-on-whose-terms/a-79673456--ab198d15d72f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-eu-wants-an-ai-revolution-but-on-whose-terms/a-79673456?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As the US and China race ahead, the European Union seeks to boost its economy with AI. Can it compete while protecting workers, safety and the climate?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Italy cuts air traffic in half amid data transmission issue</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bd0167e179acded0986d6c73805154706152870147d4bf266e492d261db7aa5b</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T10:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/italy-cuts-air-traffic-in-half-amid-data-transmission-issue/a-79678133--8d0677d89358.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/italy-cuts-air-traffic-in-half-amid-data-transmission-issue/a-79678133?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Citing problems with the data transmission network, Italian authorities have drastically reduced the volume of flights in their airspace. The ENAV authority ruled out malicious activity and said flights remained safe.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Who was Eva Mamlok? Berlin square renamed after Jewish anti-fascist resistance fighter</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:df5f8f960beff9ce8f7456041ece665ef693c998fb39e1ace2f792654a6b733c</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T09:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/who-was-eva-mamlok-berlin-square-renamed-after-jewish-anti-fascist-resistance-fighter/a-79668919--fa371a8e7f27.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/who-was-eva-mamlok-berlin-square-renamed-after-jewish-anti-fascist-resistance-fighter/a-79668919?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">She started taking action against Hitler as a teenager and never stopped until her death in a concentration camp. Berlin's Blücherplatz is now being renamed after her.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>EU promotes sovereign, trusted AI as it struggles to catch US and China</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a51620b4832c30def5c036bb7fb4e8263b897e355927ca92d88b4ac1ef6b7267</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T09:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-promotes-sovereign-trusted-ai-as-it-struggles-to-catch-us-and-china/a-79667770--286aee32e70a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-promotes-sovereign-trusted-ai-as-it-struggles-to-catch-us-and-china/a-79667770?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At an international AI summit in Dublin, EU leaders promoted trusted and independent artificial intelligence. Critics question whether the bloc can close the gap with the US and China while maintaining strict regulation.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Formula One in Rwanda: Sportswashing claims vs. hopes for African legacy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:543b318cf608ba0e336736e6a9c40514a7fadae37105f49311b4870b81162a90</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T08:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/formula-one-in-rwanda-sportswashing-claims-vs-hopes-for-african-legacy/a-79650744--59b33a158fd3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/formula-one-in-rwanda-sportswashing-claims-vs-hopes-for-african-legacy/a-79650744?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Formula One will return to Africa for the first time since 1993. There is concern Rwanda are using it as another sportswashing opportunity, but there is also hope the event's legacy can impact wider African society.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Police raid the major pro-opposition Halk TV channel in Turkey</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5eeabdf678519a8c9835e8e07960b0b4672eb6310761674ed6c766eeb332601f</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T16:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/police-raid-the-major-pro-opposition-halk-tv-channel-in-turkey/a-79671673--402c2b295200.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/police-raid-the-major-pro-opposition-halk-tv-channel-in-turkey/a-79671673?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Turkish police raided the Istanbul headquarters of an important pro-opposition television station on Wednesdazy, the day that jailed Istanbul Mayor Ekrem Imamoglu was set to start his defense against corruption charges.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>EU summit to focus on China, Ukraine and bloc budget</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2de9063dbae9ed847e6fd9f27935a7feb01eff36ebd3d84bc5fe2cf5996018b3</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T14:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-summit-to-focus-on-china-ukraine-and-bloc-budget/a-79665338--d6856904c849.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-summit-to-focus-on-china-ukraine-and-bloc-budget/a-79665338?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">EU leaders meeting in Brussels will examine measures to curb the bloc's huge trade deficit with China. But they will also be looking to further agreement on the next EU budget ahead of some major elections next year.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Romania: 2 ships on fire in Black Sea, 7 crew missing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:72568fa2cf01da9aa74cfd3ee9d2371c84bb8d16cf6d2919f4ceecaeb1764885</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T14:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/romania-2-ships-on-fire-in-black-sea-7-crew-missing/a-79667003--b330bc2c57d8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/romania-2-ships-on-fire-in-black-sea-7-crew-missing/a-79667003?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two chemical tankers have caught fire in Romanian territorial waters in the Black Sea. The blazes occurred after Russian drones were sighted in Romanian airspace.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Resignation of Bärbel Bas shines light on harsh era of German politics</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7d71fe3f095c11fe8a44b187dd5964ec3a0afa78c6fe0349d8d9af2899a78086</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T13:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/resignation-of-b_rbel-bas-shines-light-on-harsh-era-of-german-politics/a-79671395--56c0e1283306.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/resignation-of-bärbel-bas-shines-light-on-harsh-era-of-german-politics/a-79671395?maca=en-r