all is booming, but a recent report also highlights need for better structures globally.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>The hidden treasure in discarded wearable and fast tech</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:619febc60d9a7a1bdbc0c9207fe52a88115151921b89bd7976a4cf3cbebff4cf</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T06:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-hidden-treasure-in-discarded-wearable-and-fast-tech/a-79649611--7010f2eed048.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-hidden-treasure-in-discarded-wearable-and-fast-tech/a-79649611?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Sales of fast tech like mini fans and disposable e-vapes, as well as wearable health tech such as heart monitors and smartwatches are soaring. They're creating a new e-waste problem but are full of hidden treasure.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine allies in Poland after Starlink sabotage, Trump diesel deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:26324ca203670c75513990a51477dda57cc74d22179e57354196fefcfdbc63ba</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T18:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-allies-in-poland-after-starlink-sabotage-trump-diesel-deal/a-79653869--c0d0565fa8d8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-allies-in-poland-after-starlink-sabotage-trump-diesel-deal/a-79653869?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's Johann Wadephul said hybrid plots like the Starlink fire showed Europe was "in Russia's crosshairs." The UK's Ed Miliband said Trump's Russian diesel deal led to a "very difficult few days" diplomatically.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine and the US: What's next after Trump's diesel deal with Russia?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6471715f59b17a95215aa84472d59e2e484deaceda11072b978c671694036647</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T18:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-and-the-us-what-s-next-after-trump-s-diesel-deal-with-russia/a-79650785--59d833db4bc6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-and-the-us-what-s-next-after-trump-s-diesel-deal-with-russia/a-79650785?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump plans to allow the purchase of Russian diesel, drawing criticism at home and abroad. What is behind the US president's decision and what should Ukraine do next? DW spoke with experts.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Critics warn of espionage risks as Slovakia restores military-diplomatic representation with Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:631128d00dd3d7217d7c71b12ad69399eb9cf5d030311009cd70ac0042a00f09</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T12:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/critics-warn-of-espionage-risks-as-slovakia-restores-military-diplomatic-representation-with-russia/a-79649641--99619951a602.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/critics-warn-of-espionage-risks-as-slovakia-restores-military-diplomatic-representation-with-russia/a-79649641?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Slovakia is restoring military-diplomatic relations with Russia for the first time since 2022. The government has defended the move but critics warn of espionage risks and further damage to trust within NATO.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Formula 1: Rwanda to bring sport back to Africa</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fa6fbe6e64623b326e5cdf942b58a17c1e140ce2b807340091c9416252da107d</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T11:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/formula-1-rwanda-to-bring-sport-back-to-africa/a-79649217--ee284b399c6d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/formula-1-rwanda-to-bring-sport-back-to-africa/a-79649217?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The last time Formula 1 hosted a race in Africa was way back in 1993. But a new track in Rwanda is set to host a Grand Prix in "the early 2030s," continuing the country’s investment in international sport.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's China calculation shifts as import pressures eclipse export benefits</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0c915a5261b9398990b6f01b837f2131ee85ff52fe1598951dbdd0dace144b8a</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T08:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-china-calculation-shifts-as-import-pressures-eclipse-export-benefits/a-79571852--c4df7eb8a062.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-china-calculation-shifts-as-import-pressures-eclipse-export-benefits/a-79571852?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany has long resisted tougher action against China, fearing retaliation. But rising pressure on key industries has pushed Berlin to seek stronger EU trade-defense powers to protect its industrial base.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>125 years of Thomas Mann's 'Buddenbrooks'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2fd94d916fc60b81f9aaac5b55ffc3fc73a20b40aca6cdf4bcb1a93b7e8950c2</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T08:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/125-years-of-thomas-mann-s-buddenbrooks/a-44107236--20da98f1ab2b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/125-years-of-thomas-mann-s-buddenbrooks/a-44107236?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">This over 1,000-page masterpiece offers a panoramic view of society in the 19th century and exposes the collapse of a merchant family: unrecognized sons, disillusioned daughters and the loss of middle-class ideals.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>What is holding back Cyprus's Schengen ambitions?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5a6008670d740c0dc29a2b3837a42451b996f6cfcf0e11b17fb19f70332f2e3d</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T06:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-is-holding-back-cyprus-s-schengen-ambitions/a-79641488--5f69812ab764.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-is-holding-back-cyprus-s-schengen-ambitions/a-79641488?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Commission says Cyprus is ready to join the Schengen Area. Yet questions relating to the island's division and British military bases could still complicate its path to Europe's border-free travel zone.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>UK: Iran 'highly likely' to be behind RAF Fairford incident</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:338cd205c6a7dfd83cf21f1d6b1d468456151ff95dc49762d81ef382e2ca6cb1</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T19:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-iran-highly-likely-to-be-behind-raf-fairford-incident/a-79645941--7cd1b910595f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-iran-highly-likely-to-be-behind-raf-fairford-incident/a-79645941?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Andy Burnham told parliament there were "strong indications" of Iranian involvement. The government summoned Iran's ambassador. The scare at RAF Fairford led to the withdrawal of USAF B-1 heavy bombers.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Poland reports arrests of 2 Turkish citizens in Germany in connection with Starlink station fire last month</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f5c25d187086fffc2858a3533fddd88fae79381cb85b9f008b025907975db6b1</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T18:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/poland-reports-arrests-of-2-turkish-citizens-in-germany-in-connection-with-starlink-station-fire-las/a-79646138--0f2bfafb19a7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/poland-reports-arrests-of-2-turkish-citizens-in-germany-in-connection-with-starlink-station-fire-last-month/a-79646138?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Polish authorities have reported the arrests of two Turkish citizens in Germany in connection with alleged sabotage of a Starlink station last month. Prime Minister Donald Tusk called the fire an act of "hybrid warfare."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: Labor Minister's resignation puts a spotlight on cracks within the government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:de775c991e1f7cf1f10e20ca97fc5e2bc6d9f0127dda76dae5573f1d003c735d</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T17:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-labor-minister-s-resignation-puts-a-spotlight-on-cracks-within-the-government/a-79645823--1507ba6fa4a7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-labor-minister-s-resignation-puts-a-spotlight-on-cracks-within-the-government/a-79645823?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Following the sudden resignation of Bärbel Bas as Labor Minister and co-chair of the Social Democratic Party, accusations are flying in Chancellor Merz's coalition government.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Pope lung nodule: Could it be cancer?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f49e5a900afcb12e8d6b9ebe846470f6800d0622c95a42781d5bbb57ad5aba9c</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T14:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pope-lung-nodule-could-it-be-cancer/a-79641503--9cf198017761.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pope-lung-nodule-could-it-be-cancer/a-79641503?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The case of Pope Leo shows how small lung nodules are often found during routine health checks. Quick treatment is generally advised before nodules can grow to become larger life-threatening masses.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's women: Ena Mahmutovic makes her case to become Germany's next No.1 goalkeeper</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:28923f0ebe181b5b98e2a8cabef1582cc6e51cd3bcf5cce19d0aa0dff14be2a8</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T09:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-women-ena-mahmutovic-makes-her-case-to-become-germany-s-next-no-1-goalkeeper/a-79609341--71931b21638e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-women-ena-mahmutovic-makes-her-case-to-become-germany-s-next-no-1-goalkeeper/a-79609341?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's win against Australia saw Ena Mahmutovic excel in goal. The 22-year-old Bayern Munich goalkeeper is considered the successor to Ann-Katrin Berger and is making a name for herself.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>How green is Europe's urban public transport? A data-driven reality check</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e8b031beb9d4bea7863c331e494ad4929d579ff6b8a91037de4efd76692a7fdf</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T07:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-green-is-europe-s-urban-public-transport-a-data-driven-reality-check/a-79406721--a78a7db30bc7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-green-is-europe-s-urban-public-transport-a-data-driven-reality-check/a-79406721?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Greener buses and cleaner fleets are reshaping public transport across Europe. But are cities moving fast enough to meet their zero-emission goals?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>UK students call for school uniforms to be banned in pornography</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2163e52487e54d226201e786773d1769e3706b07b8de93eeeb1ae9b176e105b1</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T07:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-students-call-for-school-uniforms-to-be-banned-in-pornography/a-79554324--e21f080b6070.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-students-call-for-school-uniforms-to-be-banned-in-pornography/a-79554324?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Short skirts, knee-high socks, white blouses: Girls' school uniform items are widely used as costumes in pornographic videos. As students experience harassment, a group wants to change that.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Who are the Ukrainian 'volunteers' under Russian command?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:220931356db837317390af69d20c2b9a153fc305dc49acca5decb0a8559a7bba</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-11T18:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/who-are-the-ukrainian-volunteers-under-russian-command/a-79629555--58ee9f17fd21.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/who-are-the-ukrainian-volunteers-under-russian-command/a-79629555?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia has announced a battalion consisting of Ukrainian "volunteers." But veterans and former prisoners of war share very different accounts.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>German 'lawfare': When lawsuits become a political weapon</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dc475694a0a7d5a05eefed6f56dc7cc75f15a08115653d0b0179277843aca498</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-11T15:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-lawfare-when-lawsuits-become-a-political-weapon/a-79615817--29d1d48e91a2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-lawfare-when-lawsuits-become-a-political-weapon/a-79615817?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Left Party is suing two government ministers for accusing them of antisemitism, while Chancellor Friedrich Merz has been sued several times by various parties. Is German politics descending into "lawfare?"</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Trump claims Russia and Ukraine agreed to 'energy ceasefire'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1928705cff0dec8ada8fc7ab1fa648f42137caa77c085247f9c06932a6982aa7</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-11T14:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-claims-russia-and-ukraine-agreed-to-energy-ceasefire/a-79634509--966648814544.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-claims-russia-and-ukraine-agreed-to-energy-ceasefire/a-79634509?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump says both sides have agreed to stop targeting oil refineries, power plants and other energy infrastructure immediately.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Georgia's surrogacy industry is booming, but at what cost?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:27b989fb2eb04a74875edba9c8363a5f0e6ec335fa0464fded30cb5f864d5f57</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-11T07:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/georgia-s-surrogacy-industry-is-booming-but-at-what-cost/a-79629971--47122bb08522.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/georgia-s-surrogacy-industry-is-booming-but-at-what-cost/a-79629971?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Georgia became a hub for surrogate pregnancies after Russia's full-scale invasion of Ukraine in 2022. DW spoke with parents, and those who wanted to become parents, about the hidden costs of a booming industry.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's population is shrinking, but not everywhere</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c3b303ccd813e6e5cec74edbae59d793f137febca78800ceb7d16a2b179c3e32</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-11T07:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-population-is-shrinking-but-not-everywhere/a-79615807--3e9fde1b2ecd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-population-is-shrinking-but-not-everywhere/a-79615807?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">By 2045, Germany will have more older people, fewer workers and a smaller population overall. Yet some regions will defy this trend. Their success depends on how much they have to offer.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>'Ragebait' is the 2026 German Youth Word of the Year</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:76ebd61ed0eb9b13e2e1fb3a27d458a30b28af5ba3b24191c7c16ed89004e68c</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T13:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ragebait-is-the-2026-german-youth-word-of-the-year/a-79608158--c39c4c350c71.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ragebait-is-the-2026-german-youth-word-of-the-year/a-79608158?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Already named the 2025 Oxford Word of the Year, "rage bait" has also been widely adopted in German slang.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Operations Plan Germany: How the Bundeswehr trains for NATO collective defense</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7c3e171b1a19ea553934717a1e4cafca2b410f0819f727331a46c2f43a71deca</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T12:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/operations-plan-germany-how-the-bundeswehr-trains-for-nato-collective-defense/a-79553793--d1447370a9ee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/operations-plan-germany-how-the-bundeswehr-trains-for-nato-collective-defense/a-79553793?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">How prepared is Germany for national defense? The answer lies in the Operations Plan Germany. Military exercises such as "Red Storm Charlie" are designed to put these preparations to the test in realistic scenarios.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Author or artificial intelligence? Literature in crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:af4ab47e711a9ae96f95fb95f26329ca2e3eb5b195a2c5bd26be0fdc7554dfa4</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T15:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/author-or-artificial-intelligence-literature-in-crisis/a-79618610--2ddbca94bc5e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/author-or-artificial-intelligence-literature-in-crisis/a-79618610?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">AI is a hot topic at this year's Frankfurt Book Fair. An international literary scandal has raised questions about machine-generated texts.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Art for freedom: Maria Kalesnikava in Bonn</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b9fe52a4a24015d6bda7630994a681f873021adfdcc2372ffdf5dd655df2314b</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T13:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/art-for-freedom-maria-kalesnikava-in-bonn/a-79612009--0f2314a86e67.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/art-for-freedom-maria-kalesnikava-in-bonn/a-79612009?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Belarusian musician and civil rights activist Maria Kalesnikava held the keynote speech on the importance of art at the 2026 Beethovenfest in Bonn. She also visited DW.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>World Cup 2034: Does Saudi Arabia shelving Neom Stadium spell trouble?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5ac4e7541e59dbe32e0b7e61bae89a431b2fd0c001b6326d316d5dee5e72656a</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T11:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/world-cup-2034-does-saudi-arabia-shelving-neom-stadium-spell-trouble/a-79592948--b8b608a266b9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/world-cup-2034-does-saudi-arabia-shelving-neom-stadium-spell-trouble/a-79592948?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Since winning the right to hold the 2034 World Cup unopposed, Saudi Arabia has been pulling away from sport. With reports that its most ambitious stadium project will be abandoned, what does this mean for the World Cup?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Finland, the world's happiest nation, faces a glum winter</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f00f4b3e0736fa49f7d026af2dffc96bd885a1f98080635a7d1eacc3264c39df</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T08:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/finland-the-world-s-happiest-nation-faces-a-glum-winter/a-79544348--0df829428818.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/finland-the-world-s-happiest-nation-faces-a-glum-winter/a-79544348?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Finns have many reasons to feel content, but the country's pile of debt is not one of them. Russia's war in Ukraine has added to the fiscal burden. Can the Nordic nation absorb another shock?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>2026 Nobel Prize winner Anne Carson: Where to start reading</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:01a512b522810bd2874458b3a5653a2b54a3265f40fc9752539d19a3c9a9d5d8</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T14:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/2026-nobel-prize-winner-anne-carson-where-to-start-reading/a-79598953--08cd2959f273.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/2026-nobel-prize-winner-anne-carson-where-to-start-reading/a-79598953?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The works of this year's Nobel Prize-winning poet and essayist Anne Carson can feel slightly daunting. Here are some keys to understanding her universe.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Early-onset cancer rising worldwide: Causes, risk, prevention</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cddf3b807fc7079b33188c143796d77c4ca2e82e2313433a39a603c4853d7d0d</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T13:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/early-onset-cancer-rising-worldwide-causes-risk-prevention/a-79597097--5416293e8076.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/early-onset-cancer-rising-worldwide-causes-risk-prevention/a-79597097?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Across Latin America, early-onset cancer rates have risen, especially of bowel, breast and cervical cancers. But it is a worldwide trend.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: UK's Burnham visits Berlin for talks with Merz</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:21774393bef29fa05482d170a2febdc61b1e71f2cd79f82ac5afc6a38147e86e</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T13:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-uk-s-burnham-visits-berlin-for-talks-with-merz/live-79587637--034eb10b538b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-uk-s-burnham-visits-berlin-for-talks-with-merz/live-79587637?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">UK Prime Minister Andy Burnham is visiting Berlin to launch a new bilateral treaty and hold talks with Chancellor Friedrich Merz. President Steinmeier is on a state visit to France.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>How a multibillion-dollar oilfield has ignited the UK-Argentina feud over the Falklands</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b087cdb11b328d186450e40f134ed5db11d9e7f07e746a4de2aebcbb80714335</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T11:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-a-multibillion-dollar-oilfield-has-ignited-the-uk-argentina-feud-over-the-falklands/a-79588973--b9ae4084dbb3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-a-multibillion-dollar-oilfield-has-ignited-the-uk-argentina-feud-over-the-falklands/a-79588973?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Argentina and the UK once fought a war over the Falkland Islands. Now, the multibillion-dollar Sea Lion oil project has reignited old tensions, with Buenos Aires seeking to put a stop to the plans.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Nobel Prize in literature goes to Canada's Anne Carson</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a68eada5e0e63a4ef60882f98af7642632c3d449c07bf79b6717bee4176fd5f2</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T11:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nobel-prize-in-literature-goes-to-canada-s-anne-carson/a-79594136--7b591c2af8dd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nobel-prize-in-literature-goes-to-canada-s-anne-carson/a-79594136?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Carson won for her "bold and inventive oeuvre." The decorated poet and essayist is known for her reverence for Latin and Greek classics.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>German Bundeswehr: A new naval port in Emden aims to enhance Germany's defense capabilities</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e360533acb23b15ac369d2ddc4bad3d8f55986ff7d6ed68e44b72b2356e63017</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T09:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-bundeswehr-a-new-naval-port-in-emden-aims-to-enhance-germany-s-defense-capabilities/a-79561414--c280e8efd5f5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-bundeswehr-a-new-naval-port-in-emden-aims-to-enhance-germany-s-defense-capabilities/a-79561414?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Citing the escalating security threat, Germany's Navy has decided to establish a second port on the North Sea coast. Emden was chosen as the location.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Gerhard Schröder visits latest Russian employer, Hyperglobus</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:691d8bc4e10e0a4f607cc5b0195949b6ba99ea139fee24a03072ce4e490a1489</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T16:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gerhard-schr_der-visits-latest-russian-employer-hyperglobus/a-79583018--1d88da466f5d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gerhard-schröder-visits-latest-russian-employer-hyperglobus/a-79583018?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Former German Chancellor Gerhard Schröder visited a Moscow supermarket in his new role on the supervisory board. Schröder is no stranger to retirement stipends in Russia — or the scandal that accompanies them.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>'90s art scene in the UK: An international, edgy trendsetter</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:afeaccc778e15454eaa81138619b1c683f871fd5bdc2d8632f91eec3704b031d</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T15:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/90s-art-scene-in-the-uk-an-international-edgy-trendsetter/a-79581777--d9e1246b3502.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/90s-art-scene-in-the-uk-an-international-edgy-trendsetter/a-79581777?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The 1990s are remembered for Brit-pop and provocative fashion, but beyond the nostalgia, it was a decade of cultural experimentation and social change. Tate Britain's new exhibition looks past the familiar icons.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Merz rails against extremism, AfD sympathizers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0173f549634d111b77f3d306d175200969b9e25f41269ab48aaa6d8fde5014c9</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T15:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-rails-against-extremism-afd-sympathizers/live-79570924--74b91e3a40aa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-rails-against-extremism-afd-sympathizers/live-79570924?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Political extremism threatens Germany's existing social order, Chancellor Merz has said. The Transport Ministry has proposed a five-year plan to improve Germany's ailing railroad infrastructure.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>German spy scandal threatens national security</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f456548bb2f2c160691f5501ee7c7d0ecd235679debee8d2b90f204664b48547</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T12:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-spy-scandal-threatens-national-security/a-79580000--1e3ca23b32e3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-spy-scandal-threatens-national-security/a-79580000?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The arrest of Germany's former intelligence chief August Hanning could undermine national security, experts warn, as allies may reconsider their intelligence relationships.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: Did CDU lawmakers support the far-right AfD?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ef8ee104f2398a9ff0213739173c9651e2882fbbee066cb20c600a9a26b7e96d</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T11:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-did-cdu-lawmakers-support-the-far-right-afd/a-79577396--ed4eac4ecf1f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-did-cdu-lawmakers-support-the-far-right-afd/a-79577396?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Lawmakers of the center-right CDU may have voted for the far-right AfD candidate for parliamentary speaker in Saxony-Anhalt. Germany's Social Democrats warn of a "unique breach of taboos."</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Nobel Prize in chemistry goes to Henri B. Kagan and Kenso Soai</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f6930d0678d1b404a8a603a7665a9f7088339404f7b0a2126e394a34ba323107</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T09:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nobel-prize-in-chemistry-goes-to-henri-b-kagan-and-kenso-soai/a-79573924--1eccf7a6b469.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nobel-prize-in-chemistry-goes-to-henri-b-kagan-and-kenso-soai/a-79573924?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Henri B. Kagan and Kenso Soai won the Nobel Prize in chemistry for their groundbreaking discoveries related to the origin of chirality and life's building blocks.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Suspected pneumonic plague in Siberia: What we know about the disease</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:20169ef4795d464d9601c45890d76b18bfbae8434e1ce50a62b886a131ac60ba</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T09:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/suspected-pneumonic-plague-in-siberia-what-we-know-about-the-disease/a-79547919--6c7e74a1d6ab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/suspected-pneumonic-plague-in-siberia-what-we-know-about-the-disease/a-79547919?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After a worker at a Russian plague research institute in Siberia died October 2, 2026, nearly 200 of her contacts were under medical observation. But authorities there denied pneumonic plague had caused the death.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ronaldo stays on under cloud as Messi exits internationals</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:541453a73e2aa5337d25ec1c322906c4758970a79a13b8879d64b6ba54f07399</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T09:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ronaldo-stays-on-under-cloud-as-messi-exits-internationals/a-79574551--518c4a71824f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ronaldo-stays-on-under-cloud-as-messi-exits-internationals/a-79574551?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Just hours before Lionel Messi played his last match for Argentina, Cristiano Ronaldo posted his latest salvo in a row with Portugal. Ronaldo wants to play on despite the troubles, while Messi bathed in adulation.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Nobelitis — How winning a Nobel Prize can give you delusions of grandeur</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:07b4f3265b608d51a6a55d07e88ad117f8f8d7b0b7cae36286fa96f05f4ab919</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T08:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nobelitis-how-winning-a-nobel-prize-can-give-you-delusions-of-grandeur/a-79525772--1ee420badedc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nobelitis-how-winning-a-nobel-prize-can-give-you-delusions-of-grandeur/a-79525772?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After being chosen for one of the world's most prestigious awards, some Nobel laureates lose touch with reality and suddenly start spouting unscientific nonsense. They're afflicted by what some have called "Nobelitis."</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Emerging economies are embracing solar power and skipping fossil fuels much faster than Europe or the US</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f1fc38297532a7978aceeb1d4b27703dc858bfea58683b755693a131631924db</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T07:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/emerging-economies-are-embracing-solar-power-and-skipping-fossil-fuels-much-faster-than-europe-or-th/a-79474847--a24cf177c41d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/emerging-economies-are-embracing-solar-power-and-skipping-fossil-fuels-much-faster-than-europe-or-the-us/a-79474847?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Renewable electricity is cheaper than ever. While the West got rich on coal and oil, some of the world's poorest countries are banking on solar, wind and water instead.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Munich up against at least six competitors for 2036 Olympics</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0ae4826da172f9261dd5891695714abcb41f53c9c861d81b362b6aedfbdcc043</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T19:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/munich-up-against-at-least-six-competitors-for-2036-olympics/a-79566678--5b4a69f8bd09.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/munich-up-against-at-least-six-competitors-for-2036-olympics/a-79566678?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The International Olympic Committee has revealed the six other countries intending to bid for the 2036 Olympic Games. This comes after Germany selected Munich as its Olympic candidate.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Germany shaken by espionage and treason allegations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b47556392401828cafe4081fa5ca7ff9939dffb7272ccb0cb6e69830d8aed064</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T18:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-shaken-by-espionage-and-treason-allegations/a-79566578--c39cf46fd6f7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-shaken-by-espionage-and-treason-allegations/a-79566578?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The former head of Germany's foreign intelligence service, the BND, has been accused of spying for a foreign country. Never before has a German official of August Hanning's stature been accused of treason.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Paramount and Warner Bros merge into one Hollywood giant</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c37d5cd1a5bac594fe441b11a50a5c9383782e70f1ac92462ecd201eef35004b</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T14:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/paramount-and-warner-bros-merge-into-one-hollywood-giant/a-79565762--fd1d53153557.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/paramount-and-warner-bros-merge-into-one-hollywood-giant/a-79565762?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Paramount has completed an $81 billion purchase of Warner Bros. Discovery, as its owner Skydance creates a new entertainment behemoth. Billionaire David Ellison's hostile takeover bid defeated rival efforts from Netflix.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's far-right AfD makes history again in Saxony-Anhalt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7a28b0200bb102bed8398022b7fb55ca1047ddbc2cf9ab3cb5a68099a457dc72</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T13:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-far-right-afd-makes-history-again-in-saxony-anhalt/a-79565146--3b11bbf1dc05.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-far-right-afd-makes-history-again-in-saxony-anhalt/a-79565146?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">For the first time since the end of World War II, a German state parliament has chosen parliamentary speaker from the far right: Tobias Rausch of the Alternative for Germany (AfD).</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Nobel Prize in literature: How the winner is secretly chosen</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f99ce1f0b02de4aaa52675a689fbd1f6cb388abb8155116f80db894fdd61890e</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T13:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nobel-prize-in-literature-how-the-winner-is-secretly-chosen/a-79564151--0152f72654ee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nobel-prize-in-literature-how-the-winner-is-secretly-chosen/a-79564151?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Can Xue is considered one of this year's favorites; Margaret Atwood and Salman Rushdie are other strong contenders. But what goes on behind the scenes in the selection of the Nobel Prize in literature?</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>AI models keep hacking real systems during tests. What does this mean?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9da90a1a220ffba847fce7aba8967343af57a61000e091e632533b9ee1c1edc1</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T10:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ai-models-keep-hacking-real-systems-during-tests-what-does-this-mean/a-79471943--07f5722af213.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ai-models-keep-hacking-real-systems-during-tests-what-does-this-mean/a-79471943?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">AI models have repeatedly broken into real commercial and government systems during safety tests during 2026. Cybersecurity researcher Thorsten Holz explains what that means, and why he isn't expecting a robot uprising.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Merz, Macron seek tougher EU measures against unfair trade</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0ee16ff86d9ece07d6c291b50a6d6be6161092ad9ee03b7175607644f6d69aa3</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T17:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/merz-macron-seek-tougher-eu-measures-against-unfair-trade/a-79554905--9b126d039a17.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/merz-macron-seek-tougher-eu-measures-against-unfair-trade/a-79554905?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Emmanuel Macron and Friedrich Merz have written to Ursula von der Leyen, calling for tougher EU mechanisms against unfair trade practices by other states. They name no names but seem to have China or the US in mind.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Euro plummets against US dollar: Has the next financial crisis begun?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cd601e06d1491c77b6c57034e086864eee3fa432b203b4f4e4d2365f095e1520</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T14:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/euro-plummets-against-us-dollar-has-the-next-financial-crisis-begun/a-79549031--86ee12acb8f2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/euro-plummets-against-us-dollar-has-the-next-financial-crisis-begun/a-79549031?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The euro has fallen to a 17-month low against the dollar. That will make inflation worse in the EU, where political worries and concern over French debt are already troubling investors. Is a fiscal crisis at hand?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Jürgen Klopp faces myriad of issues after rough start with Germany</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e4a1d950e70153cbcd82376860cdff8a59e02a822e15eeee647c0ce3d38539db</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T10:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/j_rgen-klopp-faces-myriad-of-issues-after-rough-start-with-germany/a-79547308--c13c1fe885bf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/jürgen-klopp-faces-myriad-of-issues-after-rough-start-with-germany/a-79547308?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Jürgen Klopp has done things a little differently since becoming Germany coach. Casting a wider net for talent and trying to connect with players and country haven't made an immediate impact, but he is not bowed.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>"NAZA": Israeli military issues statement on film</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:638cbc3d544beef77a3d472da8d55748c51ca531e4ffae1283787b2fce126f37</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T15:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/naza-israeli-military-issues-statement-on-film/a-79520483--c29108607d5e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/naza-israeli-military-issues-statement-on-film/a-79520483?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The award-winning documentary "NAZA" continues to spark controversy in Israel. The Israeli military has now published a multi-page statement calling the film's portrayal "distorted."</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Franz Reindl elected new IIHF president</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3f2d677bac1492e5b5a51db73f5288e77be83d82425bdcfa7e53fd3e89dfec42</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T14:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-franz-reindl-elected-new-iihf-president/a-79521799--24f017ae08ee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-franz-reindl-elected-new-iihf-president/a-79521799?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Franz Reindl has been elected president of ice hockey's world governing body. The former forward was a member of West Germany's Olympic bronze medal-winning team.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Climate leaders called for solar energy for 'everyone, everywhere' by 2030, but with three years to go, is that goal attainable?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9eee53c207d19f6e38a7c6d9e67c22c23fcd2a39afa7ed3bd61f843b8565fb4c</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T13:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/climate-leaders-called-for-solar-energy-for-everyone-everywhere-by-2030-but-with-three-years-to-go-i/a-79517056--052584d0bcdc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/climate-leaders-called-for-solar-energy-for-everyone-everywhere-by-2030-but-with-three-years-to-go-is-that-goal-attainable/a-79517056?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Prominent climate leaders have called on governments, businesses, institutions and the public to make a push for solar power before the decade is out, repowering the world with cheap, clean energy. Is that possible?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Manchester City Premier League charges: What do they mean?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bc2f4e75352184c06cbe59c81753e6cdbfde354cbfc59359cefe94088e5c1df9</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T11:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/manchester-city-premier-league-charges-what-do-they-mean/a-79485638--5f423a99075f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/manchester-city-premier-league-charges-what-do-they-mean/a-79485638?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Since being bought by the UAE in 2008, Manchester City has become one of the world's most successful football clubs. A raft of serious financial charges threatens to undermine this and bring chaos to the Premier League.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey: Stock market scandal hits half a million investors</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ebcca026235c96e210ba0d9705f3d06e2b8de1c28786efd771f802df1c421ad5</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T04:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/turkey-stock-market-scandal-hits-half-a-million-investors/a-79494710--a0311f00dcbd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/turkey-stock-market-scandal-hits-half-a-million-investors/a-79494710?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Asset managers are alleged to have artificially inflated the value of their funds. Turkish authorities have made multiple arrests, and a leading AKP lawmaker has resigned.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Klopp wins first game as Germany coach, without 'top dogs'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9c0a4939879bf49e0f07ddcf0cb9f30b4fce128e97cb7336b9a97027d56d037c</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T22:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/klopp-wins-first-game-as-germany-coach-without-top-dogs/a-79508898--6c1fca750e8a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/klopp-wins-first-game-as-germany-coach-without-top-dogs/a-79508898?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">It may have taken a little longer than he would have liked, but Jürgen Klopp has finally won a game as Germany coach. Despite a number of debutants, it was a familiar face who stood out in the victory over Serbia.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry>